@version 2

RecordFrequency 100
RecordAll True

MaxSteps 301

MinAgents 20
MaxAgents 25
InitAgents MaxAgents

MinFood 10
MaxFood 30

MaxInternalNeuralGroups 5

WorldSize 25

################################################################################
#
# Agent Metabolisms
#
#   W1h residual 3 (t_a0aca481).  Derivation of native
#   `tests/low-spec-pc/minitest.wf`: identical except for this section, which
#   defines TWO metabolisms so that
#
#     * `Simulation::getStatusText` prints the per-metabolism alive counts
#       (` -<Name> = <n>`, printed only when
#       `Metabolism::getNumberOfDefinitions() > 1`, Simulation.cc:4894-4904);
#     * the populations actually split, so the metabolism count is a different
#       number from the status text's `agents` count -- which is what makes the
#       recording able to distinguish the two.
#
#   Selection mode `Random`: `agent::setGenomeReady()` draws
#   `index = nint( (getNumberOfDefinitions() - 1) * drand() )` (agent.cc:490-505)
#   for every agent, including newborns, so the split is ~50/50 and stable.
#   The default mode (`Gene`) would key the metabolism off a genome gene.
#
#   Names differ (the native auto-rename to `MetabolismN` applies only to a
#   `Null` name, Simulation.cc:4082-4087), and both keep the schema's default
#   `EnergyPolarity [ 1 ]` / `EnergyDelta [ 0 ]` / `CarcassFoodTypeMode
#   FindEnergyPolarity` -- the metabolism *identity* is what this fixture is
#   about, not its energy semantics.
#
################################################################################
AgentMetabolisms
[
  {
    Name  "Alpha"
  }
  ,
  {
    Name  "Beta"
  }
]

AgentMetabolismSelectionMode Random
